  "summary": "Reconciled Walter Kim's (pt-0005) medications after his St. Brigid discharge, per RBC-TOC-02. Sources: discharge summary doc-00025, signed addendum doc-00026, and the Northgate BMP from 10/21 (doc-00027): potassium 5.4 (high), creatinine 1.32.\nChanges:\n- Furosemide: dose raised from 20 to 40 mg daily. The old order mr-00076 was changed and replaced by mr-t0001.\n- Potassium chloride: stopped (mr-00075).\nNo change:\n- Metoprolol XL 50 mg: another name for his existing metoprolol succinate ER 50 mg order (mr-00074).\n- Atorvastatin and aspirin: continued as before.\n- Omeprazole: kept. The hospital gave pantoprazole only as a formulary swap, so it wasn't ordered.\nNot started or resumed because potassium is 5.4, above the 5.0 cutoff in §7:\n- Lisinopril: stays on hold (mr-00073). This is despite creatinine 1.32 meeting the discharge condition to resume it (creatinine below 1.5).\n- Spironolactone 25 mg: not ordered. The dose is 25 mg per the addendum's correction of 12.5 mg.\n- A task for Dr. Okafor (task-t0003), due 10/26, covers reviewing the repeat potassium and deciding on both drugs.\nFlagged to Dr. Okafor (message comm-t0004): the discharge documents don't mention home metoprolol tartrate 25 mg twice daily (mr-00071), so I left it unchanged. He also has the metoprolol succinate order, so this may be a duplicate beta-blocker.\nThe progress note documenting all of this is doc-t0005.",
